  "ans": "D",
  "exp": "Packet switching breaks data into packets that share a common communications channel with many other users' traffic (statistical multiplexing), rather than dedicating a circuit end-to-end. Because the channel is shared rather than reserved, the per-user cost of accessing shared information utilities/networks falls -- so both (b) and (c) are true properties, making (d) correct. Option (a) is wrong because packet-switched networks are not free to build or operate; they simply share cost across users.",
