  "sub": "Software Testing Strategies: Organizing for software testing",
  "q": "Which of the following issue/issues must be addressed if a successful software testing strategy is to be implemented?\ni. Use effective formal technical reviews as a filter prior to testing\nii. Develop a testing plan that emphasizes \"rapid cycle testing\"\niii. State testing objectives explicitly",
  "opts": {
   "A": "i only",
   "B": "ii only",
   "C": "ii and iii only",
   "D": "i, ii and iii"
  },
  "ans": "D",
  "exp": "All three listed items are drawn directly from the classic Pressman list of issues that must be addressed for a successful software-testing strategy: conducting formal technical reviews before testing begins filters out many defects cheaply; building a plan around rapid-cycle testing catches issues early and iteratively; and explicitly stating testing objectives ensures the test effort is measurable and goal-directed. Since none of the three statements is false or extraneous, the only option that credits all of them, D, is correct; the partial options (A, B, C) each wrongly exclude at least one genuinely necessary practice.",
  "prov": "Official MPSC final answer key",
