  "ans": "B",
  "exp": "Starting from a Class C network (default mask 255.255.255.0), we need enough subnet bits for >=5 subnets and enough host bits for >=16 hosts each. Mask .224 (11100000) borrows 3 bits for subnetting (up to 8 subnets, well over 5) and leaves 5 host bits, giving 2^5-2=30 usable hosts per subnet, satisfying both requirements. Mask .240 (option c) leaves only 4 host bits (2^4-2=14 hosts), which fails the \"at least 16 hosts\" requirement. Mask .192 (option a) gives only 2 subnet bits (up to 4 subnets), too few for 5 subnets. Mask .248 (option d) leaves just 3 host bits (6 hosts), also too few.",
