  "sub": "Database design, functional dependencies and normal forms",
  "q": "Which of the following is a transitive dependency?",
  "opts": {
   "A": "A functional dependency between two or more key attributes.",
   "B": "A functional dependency between two or more nonkey attributes.",
   "C": "A relation that is in first normal form.",
   "D": "A relation that is in second normal form."
  },
  "ans": "B",
  "exp": "A transitive dependency exists when a non-key attribute depends on another non-key attribute (X -> Y -> Z, where Y and Z are both non-key), rather than depending directly on the primary key. Option (A) describes a dependency among key attributes, which is not transitive by definition. Options (C) and (D) describe normal forms, not dependencies themselves -- 3NF is specifically the normal form defined as having no transitive dependencies, which is a related but different concept from the dependency itself.",
