  "exp": "This is the standard definition of a superkey: any set of one or more attributes whose values, taken together, uniquely identify a tuple -- with no requirement that it be minimal. A candidate key (A) is a stricter concept: a superkey with the additional property of minimality (no attribute can be removed without losing uniqueness). Since the question's wording omits any minimality requirement, it matches superkey rather than candidate key. A foreign key (D) references another relation's key and is unrelated to uniqueness within its own table; 'sub key' is not a standard relational-model term.",
