  "exp": "Corrective regression testing is used when a defect fix changes only the source code while the specification stays the same, so existing test cases can be reused as-is. Progressive regression testing is used when the specification itself changes (new or modified requirements), requiring new test cases to be designed alongside the code changes. So the blanks read: Corrective (source-code-only change) ... progressive (specification-driven change), matching option (B). Option (A) reverses the pairing, and 'incremental/unincremental' (C) are not standard regression-testing terms.",
