  "sub": "Process management",
  "q": "The following program: main() { if(fork()>0) sleep(100); } results in the creation of",
  "opts": {
   "A": "an orphan process",
   "B": "a zombie process",
   "C": "a process that executes forever",
   "D": "None of these"
  },
  "ans": "B",
  "exp": "fork()>0 is true only in the parent, which then sleeps for 100 seconds without ever calling wait(). The child (where fork() returns 0) skips the sleep, finishes main() almost immediately, and terminates -- but since its sleeping parent hasn't reaped its exit status, the child sits as a zombie for the duration of the parent's sleep.",
  "conf": "high",
  "prov": "Jr. Grade of MES, November 2015, Paper II, Q3; answer derived by review - no official key exists for this sitting",
  "note": "Only the Paper-I-syllabus questions from this paper were imported (10 of 49)."
