  "sub": "Sequential circuit states",
  "q": "How will you define the present state and next state of sequential circuit?",
  "opts": {},
  "ans": "",
  "model": "In a clocked sequential circuit the flip-flops are the memory, and their combined contents are the state. The present state is the vector of flip-flop outputs at time t — the value stored just before the active clock edge — written Q(t). The next state is the value that same vector takes immediately after that edge, Q(t+1). Only the clock transition can change one into the other; between edges the present state is held.\n\nThe next state is a function of the present state and the current inputs: Q(t+1) = f(Q(t), X). In practice you write the excitation equations for the flip-flop inputs and combine them with the flip-flop characteristic equation — for a D flip-flop Q(t+1) = D, for JK Q(t+1) = J·Q' + K'·Q — to get the state equations.\n\nMano's two-flip-flop example: A(t+1) = A·x + B·x, B(t+1) = A'·x, y = (A + B)·x'. If the present state is AB = 00 with input x = 1, then A(t+1) = 0·1 + 0·1 = 0 and B(t+1) = 1·1 = 1, so the next state is AB = 01, and the output y = (0+0)·0 = 0.\n\nTabulating this for every present-state/input pair gives the state table; drawn as circles joined by labelled arrows it is the state diagram.",
  "points": [
   "Present state = flip-flop contents Q(t) just before the active clock edge",
   "Next state = Q(t+1), the contents just after the edge; changes only on the clock transition",
   "Next state is a function of present state and inputs: Q(t+1) = f(Q(t), X)",
   "Derives it from the excitation equations plus the flip-flop characteristic equation (D: Q(t+1)=D; JK: Q(t+1)=JQ'+K'Q)",
   "Works one transition: present AB = 00, x = 1 gives next AB = 01",
   "Connects to the state table / state diagram, and to Moore vs Mealy output dependence"
  ],
  "exp": "",
  "conf": "high",
  "prov": "Jr. Grade of MES, P&E Cadre (Electrical Wing), July 2023, Paper I, Section B Q9; conventional short-answer question (5 marks) - model answer written for this app; no official MPSC answer exists for it",
