  "sectionB": true,
  "paper": "TECH1",
  "unit": "2",
  "sub": "Carry lookahead adder",
  "q": "Why look ahead carry adder is faster than ripple adder?",
  "opts": {},
  "ans": "",
  "model": "In an n-bit ripple carry adder the full adders are chained: stage i cannot produce its sum until carry C_i has arrived from stage i-1. The carry path through one full adder costs about 2 gate delays, so the final carry C_n settles only after roughly 2n gate delays. The addition time therefore grows linearly with the word length.\n\nCarry lookahead breaks the chain by computing every carry directly from the operands. Per bit define generate G_i = A_i·B_i and propagate P_i = A_i ⊕ B_i. Then C_(i+1) = G_i + P_i·C_i, and unrolling the recursion removes the dependence on the previous carry:\nC1 = G0 + P0·C0\nC2 = G1 + P1·G0 + P1·P0·C0\nC3 = G2 + P2·G1 + P2·P1·G0 + P2·P1·P0·C0\nC4 = G3 + P3·G2 + P3·P2·G1 + P3·P2·P1·G0 + P3·P2·P1·P0·C0\n\nEvery carry is now a two-level AND-OR function of the inputs and C0 alone, so all carries appear at the same instant, after a delay that does not depend on n.\n\nTiming for 4 bits: ripple = 2 × 4 = 8 gate delays to C4; lookahead = 1 (P,G) + 2 (AND-OR carry) + 1 (S_i = P_i ⊕ C_i) = 4. At 16 bits ripple needs about 32 while lookahead stays near 4. The price is many more gates and high fan-in, which is why wide adders use hierarchical 4-bit lookahead blocks.",
  "points": [
   "Ripple carry is serial: carry propagates stage by stage, worst case ≈ 2n gate delays",
   "Defines G_i = A_i·B_i, P_i = A_i ⊕ B_i and the recursion C_(i+1) = G_i + P_i·C_i",
   "Unrolls to give C1..C4 as two-level AND-OR expressions of the inputs and C0 only",
   "All carries generated in parallel, so delay is constant and independent of n",
   "Quantifies: 4-bit ripple ≈ 8 gate delays vs lookahead ≈ 4; 16-bit ≈ 32 vs ≈ 4",
   "Notes the cost: more gates and higher fan-in, hence hierarchical lookahead for wide adders"
  ],
  "exp": "",
  "conf": "high",
  "prov": "Jr. Grade of MES, P&E Cadre (Electrical Wing), July 2023, Paper I, Section B Q10; conventional short-answer question (5 marks) - model answer written for this app; no official MPSC answer exists for it",
  "note": "Model answer"
